WEBVTT

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:12.970
I want Giuse-san to care for
me even more than he does now.

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:22.340
Would saying that make him not like me?

00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:29.680
I know I'm treated much
nicer than all the other girls!

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:36.130
Dr. Bianchi. Am I being selfish?

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.140
Don't worry.

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:48.740
There's nothing wrong
with feeling that at all.

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:55.180
Giuse-niisama!

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:59.220
Is it true you're going to the Balkans?!

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:02.260
It'll only be for half a year.
I'll be back soon.

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:08.490
Don't go! They say it's
dangerous because of the radiation!

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:14.300
You won't be lonely.
Our brother will still be here.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:21.140
But... Jean-niisama is too
busy to ever come to my recitals.

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:25.110
Father and Mother and Jean-niisama...

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:28.920
Work is more important to them than me.

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:32.590
They always leave me all alone at home.

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:35.020
That's not true.

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:40.400
They all love you the most.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:44.070
When I grow up, I'm going
to join the military police!

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:47.200
That way, we'll always be togeth...!

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:51.710
It's very dangerous to be an
M.P. In this country right now.

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:56.140
You should be a harp soloist, Enrica.

00:01:57.150 --> 00:02:04.620
Amid the difficulty of
sticking to that one feeling,

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:19.490
I want to protect you and fulfill
my promise to the only one for me

00:02:19.670 --> 00:02:27.180
In a world filled with doubt,
I still can't find the answer

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:34.350
Even so, I continue forward... Why?

00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:44.730
If I can change this dream-like
reality with my own two hands,

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:52.370
amid the difficulty of
sticking to that one feeling,

00:02:52.370 --> 00:03:00.080
I want to protect the only one for me

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:07.780
I swear on my beating heart I will
continue to run until I burn away

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:15.190
Amid the eternal love I feel simply by living,

00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:24.000
I want to fulfill my promise

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:48.120
Just a dream...

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:50.960
Are you up, Giuse?

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:53.530
Go to bed if you're going to sleep.

00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:55.960
Yeah, Brother.

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:01.270
I'm meeting Marcantonio tomorrow.

00:04:01.270 --> 00:04:04.310
Your old friend Second Lieutenant Abbado?

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:06.410
How many years has it been?

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:11.310
Five or six years since I
got my discharge, I guess...

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:17.400
"Clever Snake, Simple Pigeon"

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:27.360
Whoa, Giuse. You grew your hair out.

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:30.470
What do you do these days? PMC?

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:34.840
No, an acquaintance of mine
hooked me up with a public welfare job.

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:35.970
Public welfare?

00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:36.910
Is that strange?

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:38.400
Yeah!

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:43.010
That incident must've
been pretty hard on you...

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:46.820
Yeah... it was.

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:49.320
The news back then was crazy.

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:54.520
I can understand why you and
your brother quit the military police.

00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:01.000
How are things with you, Marcantonio?

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.830
I assume you're still with
the 1st Parachute Regiment?

00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:08.070
Me? I'm leader of a patrol squad in Molise.

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:11.310
I crack down on
smuggling and kidnappings.

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:14.710
You? Commander of a
reconnaissance squad?

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:16.410
Is that funny?

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:20.350
I wound up with the job because you left.

00:05:20.350 --> 00:05:26.410
I had it easy while you were
head of the class in the Balkans PKF.

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:34.260
How's your mom?

00:05:34.260 --> 00:05:38.860
She always used to make
us salsiccia at your place.

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:41.830
She's dead.

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:47.640
The year before last, she took
part in a citizens' demonstration.

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:51.480
An officer's tear gas
grenade hit her on the head...

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:54.010
I had no idea...

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:08.660
Didn't your sister play the harp too?

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:10.530
Yeah...

00:06:30.220 --> 00:06:32.850
- A terrorist attack?!
- Yeah!

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:44.560
You all right?! Pull yourself together! Hey!

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:07.120
Shit!

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:10.590
Beatrice. He's headed
your way. Hold him up.

00:07:10.590 --> 00:07:12.650
Understood.

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:27.480
Hey, Beace. Check his smell.

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:29.570
Yes, sir.

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:35.420
He smells of military explosives.

00:07:35.420 --> 00:07:39.420
So you're the one behind
yesterday's terrorist bombing?

00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:41.560
Do you want to suffer?

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:45.890
Now, now, Jean-san.
Let's just go check out his place.

00:07:45.890 --> 00:07:48.530
He's a blue... a Padania.

00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:52.190
In which case, there's
gotta be some evidence.

00:08:07.180 --> 00:08:09.450
Oh, did you find it?

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:10.920
Yes, sir.

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:12.390
Here.

00:08:24.130 --> 00:08:26.300
Where did you obtain this?

00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:30.700
Only military men can get their
hands on such high-grade explosives.

00:08:32.010 --> 00:08:33.040
Rico.

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:35.710
Yes, Jean-san?

00:08:35.710 --> 00:08:38.680
Make him hurt, until he decides to talk.

00:08:38.680 --> 00:08:40.510
Yes, sir!

00:08:54.030 --> 00:08:55.530
Poor guy.

00:08:55.530 --> 00:08:58.100
The possession of
explosives is a serious offense.

00:08:58.100 --> 00:09:01.540
He can regret it behind bars.

00:09:11.180 --> 00:09:15.840
Punch 'im all you want, but there's
no way to bring back the dead...

00:09:17.090 --> 00:09:21.080
"Castel Sant'Angelo, Rome"

00:09:32.370 --> 00:09:33.470
Giuse-san!

00:09:33.470 --> 00:09:36.770
Is that the river Princess Ann swam in?!

00:09:36.770 --> 00:09:39.070
That's right.

00:09:39.070 --> 00:09:43.050
Then is that bridge where
she fought using the guitar?!

00:09:43.050 --> 00:09:46.040
Yeah, that's right.

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:50.890
Castel Sant'Angelo... What a pretty castle!

00:09:50.890 --> 00:09:53.890
As I recall, "Tosca" also
takes place in this castle.

00:09:53.890 --> 00:09:55.790
Tosca?

00:09:55.790 --> 00:09:57.560
It's an opera.

00:09:57.560 --> 00:10:01.590
The last scene takes
place by that big angel statue.

00:10:10.140 --> 00:10:15.310
Colonel Gagne supervises
military logistics in Molise.

00:10:15.310 --> 00:10:17.310
There've been nasty rumors for some time

00:10:17.310 --> 00:10:20.180
that he's been putting
weapons on the black market.

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:24.820
The Padania has been
well-armed since the start of this year.

00:10:24.820 --> 00:10:28.890
We even recovered large amounts
of military explosives last week.

00:10:28.890 --> 00:10:30.190
Proof.

00:10:30.190 --> 00:10:31.930
If we can just have proof,

00:10:31.930 --> 00:10:35.100
the military police will silently
approve the colonel's assassination.

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:37.760
Understood.

00:10:42.770 --> 00:10:44.940
When will it ever end?

00:10:44.940 --> 00:10:47.610
When will what end, Lieutenant Colonel?

00:10:47.610 --> 00:10:49.950
The fighting.

00:10:49.950 --> 00:10:52.410
Do you remember the Balkans conflict?

00:10:52.410 --> 00:10:56.750
We fought under those
gray skies for two whole years.

00:10:56.750 --> 00:11:01.620
But at the time, we didn't even
know who we were fighting with.

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:07.560
It was an ethnic conflict.
Every armed militant was an enemy.

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:12.470
No. The enemy was hate itself.

00:11:12.470 --> 00:11:16.960
So it's no wonder we left
with nothing to show for it.

00:11:18.170 --> 00:11:22.780
Hate can never be beaten down forever.

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:26.280
The end will come someday.

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:29.380
Is that what you believe?

00:11:29.380 --> 00:11:34.520
What other choice is there than to fight?

00:11:35.520 --> 00:11:40.660
Indeed. That is all we can do.

00:11:43.170 --> 00:11:44.670
Castel Sant'Angelo?

00:11:44.670 --> 00:11:49.500
Yeah. Henrietta loves Princess Ann,
so she really enjoyed it.

00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:52.410
I'd say "Tosca" better
represents Sant'Angelo.

00:11:52.410 --> 00:11:55.480
The opera? Did you see it on video?

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:56.810
Yes.

00:11:57.750 --> 00:12:01.350
I bet Henrietta would cry if she heard it.

00:12:01.350 --> 00:12:05.190
Like, "I lived on art, I lived on love..."

00:12:05.190 --> 00:12:07.280
How does it go?

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:18.830
"I lived on art, I lived on love,
never have I harmed a single soul."

00:12:18.830 --> 00:12:24.870
"Whenever my misery was known,
a helping hand was there for me."

00:12:24.870 --> 00:12:34.370
"But, now, in my suffering,
why do you make justice this way, Lord?"

00:12:35.780 --> 00:12:39.520
"For all my life I have
adorned the Blessed Virgin

00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:43.720
and offered songs to the stars."

00:12:46.970 --> 00:12:49.330
"Palazzo Farnese Plaza, Rome"

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:51.310
"Palazzo Farnese Plaza, Rome"
Tosca takes place 200 years ago,

00:12:51.310 --> 00:12:51.900
Tosca takes place 200 years ago,

00:12:51.900 --> 00:12:54.200
when Rome is under a reign of terror.

00:12:54.200 --> 00:12:56.740
The main character is a
songstress named Tosca.

00:12:56.740 --> 00:13:02.340
Her lover is given a death sentence
for sheltering a political criminal.

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:06.680
Tosca goes to the police
commissioner to beg for his life.

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:08.020
That's the basic premise.

00:13:08.020 --> 00:13:11.990
You know a lot about it. Do you like opera?

00:13:11.990 --> 00:13:15.460
Me? I'm not the type.

00:13:15.460 --> 00:13:19.360
I saw it with an acquaintance
a long time ago, that's all.

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:21.000
"Sant'Andrea della Valle, Rome"

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:25.120
"Sant'Andrea della Valle, Rome"
All of the main characters in
Tosca wind up dying in the end.

00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:25.500
All of the main characters in
Tosca wind up dying in the end.

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:28.100
Same happens in all Italian operas.

00:13:28.100 --> 00:13:33.380
Illness, suicide, revenge...
People just die and die!

00:13:33.380 --> 00:13:36.540
Do you know what that means, Beace?

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:37.700
No.

00:13:38.780 --> 00:13:45.690
Basically means Italians love
tragedy and are sentimental about death!

00:13:47.790 --> 00:13:51.730
That's why our cities are
filled with violence and revenge,

00:13:51.730 --> 00:13:56.750
and why we can't solve
anything without shedding blood!

00:14:08.880 --> 00:14:13.080
Say, Bianchi. It's been
tiring me more and more lately.

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:14.520
What has?

00:14:14.520 --> 00:14:19.490
The only things Henrietta and I
can talk about are stars and myths.

00:14:19.490 --> 00:14:25.290
And all the presents are out of
formality... rather than sincerity.

00:14:25.290 --> 00:14:30.070
What's wrong about that?
She's starved for love.

00:14:30.070 --> 00:14:33.730
What's so wrong with fulfilling that need?

00:14:35.170 --> 00:14:37.170
What's wrong, Giuse?

00:14:37.170 --> 00:14:40.680
My little sister was always home all alone.

00:14:40.680 --> 00:14:44.870
We were all too busy with our own affairs.

00:14:45.910 --> 00:14:48.750
We made her feel lonely...

00:14:48.750 --> 00:14:51.590
And you wish you could take it back?

00:14:51.590 --> 00:14:53.280
Yeah.

00:14:54.260 --> 00:14:59.330
"Be clever like a snake,
simple like a pigeon."

00:14:59.330 --> 00:15:01.420
What's that?

00:15:03.260 --> 00:15:07.100
An attitude to survive this harsh world.

00:15:07.870 --> 00:15:11.100
Easier said than done, though.

00:15:11.410 --> 00:15:14.930
There's nothing wrong with
thinking things over delicately.

00:15:15.240 --> 00:15:19.700
There's no need to feel
shame in acting shrewdly.

00:15:20.580 --> 00:15:22.150
The answer's simple.

00:15:22.150 --> 00:15:27.050
Basically... don't think about it so hard.

00:15:30.660 --> 00:15:32.680
Yeah.

00:15:41.570 --> 00:15:45.710
Jean-san. The army
truck is through the pass.

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:50.110
Understood, Ferro.
Stop all subsequent vehicles.

00:15:50.110 --> 00:15:52.340
Roger.

00:15:55.150 --> 00:15:58.140
So, are we going to capture them?

00:15:59.250 --> 00:16:01.590
If they listen to our warning.

00:16:01.590 --> 00:16:06.580
Even if we kill them,
the scene itself should serve as proof.

00:16:13.970 --> 00:16:15.470
Sir!

00:16:15.470 --> 00:16:17.560
Stop the truck!

00:16:19.010 --> 00:16:20.010
Don't move!

00:16:20.010 --> 00:16:23.550
Stop the engine and state
your ranks, names, and cargo!

00:16:23.550 --> 00:16:25.210
Back up!

00:16:28.850 --> 00:16:30.780
Hirscher! Do it!

00:16:46.030 --> 00:16:48.940
- Rico!
- Yes, sir.

00:17:38.790 --> 00:17:40.960
Giuse-san! What did you think?

00:17:40.960 --> 00:17:44.790
I thought I shot rather... well...

00:17:44.790 --> 00:17:46.490
Yeah...

00:18:01.910 --> 00:18:04.310
Turn.

00:18:05.910 --> 00:18:08.250
And turn again.

00:18:09.680 --> 00:18:11.590
It's not too tight, is it?

00:18:11.590 --> 00:18:12.790
No.

00:18:12.790 --> 00:18:13.760
And your shoulders?

00:18:13.760 --> 00:18:16.990
They're fine.

00:18:16.990 --> 00:18:19.830
Have you changed clothes, Henrietta?

00:18:19.830 --> 00:18:21.130
Yeah.

00:18:21.130 --> 00:18:25.070
Skirts are neat, huh?
Your legs make a swish-swish sound!

00:18:25.070 --> 00:18:29.140
It seems Marcantonio blamed the
government for his mother's death

00:18:29.140 --> 00:18:31.510
and turned traitor.

00:18:31.510 --> 00:18:33.640
He assembled squad
members with similar motives

00:18:33.640 --> 00:18:38.580
and worked for Colonel Gagne
smuggling weapons while off-duty.

00:18:39.750 --> 00:18:42.420
The colonel's assassination
has been approved.

00:18:42.420 --> 00:18:47.290
We'll do it when he comes
to see an opera next week.

00:18:47.290 --> 00:18:48.820
Got it.

00:18:48.820 --> 00:18:53.590
Giuse. I can do it on my own, if you'd like.

00:18:56.000 --> 00:19:01.270
I'll be fine. It's not worth
getting depressed over now.

00:19:01.270 --> 00:19:04.200
Yeah. Exactly.

00:19:10.510 --> 00:19:14.740
Clever like a snake, huh...

00:19:17.280 --> 00:19:21.580
"Rome Opera House"

00:20:03.230 --> 00:20:08.000
There's nothing wrong with
thinking things over delicately.

00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:12.370
There's no need to feel
shame in acting shrewdly.

00:20:12.370 --> 00:20:15.140
Umm, Giuse-san...

00:20:33.260 --> 00:20:35.330
You look beautiful.

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:37.770
Giuse-san...

00:20:37.770 --> 00:20:39.270
Now go on.

00:20:39.270 --> 00:20:41.200
Yes, sir!

00:22:04.350 --> 00:22:05.920
We're home!

00:22:05.920 --> 00:22:08.890
Welcome back. How was the opera?

00:22:08.890 --> 00:22:12.230
We didn't see much
because we were working.

00:22:12.230 --> 00:22:14.300
Oh, I should've figured.

00:22:14.300 --> 00:22:17.500
That's too bad.
It's such a moving story, too.

00:22:17.500 --> 00:22:20.970
I only got to see the first part.

00:22:20.970 --> 00:22:23.370
Say, Rico.

00:22:23.370 --> 00:22:25.470
Were you moved?

00:22:25.470 --> 00:22:29.000
It scared me how loud it was!

00:22:30.410 --> 00:22:36.250
Hey, Rico! Guess what!
Giuse-san said this dress looks beautiful!

00:22:36.250 --> 00:22:38.320
That's great, Henrietta!

00:22:38.320 --> 00:22:42.420
Jean-san only told me, "It doesn't suit you."

00:22:42.420 --> 00:22:47.690
"I lived on art, I lived on love..."

00:22:53.870 --> 00:22:58.310
What'd you think of the opera, Enrica?
Are you still too young for it?

00:22:58.310 --> 00:23:00.680
No, I really liked it!

00:23:00.680 --> 00:23:03.510
Really? That's great!

00:23:03.510 --> 00:23:07.280
Giuse-niisama!
I'm going to be a harp soloist!

00:23:07.280 --> 00:23:10.550
Someday, I'm going to
play my harp in this theater!

00:23:10.550 --> 00:23:14.360
Really? I can't wait!

00:23:14.360 --> 00:23:15.360
When that day comes,

00:23:15.360 --> 00:23:20.030
you and Mother and Father
all have to come, okay?!

00:23:20.030 --> 00:23:24.330
Yeah! It's a promise!

00:23:43.750 --> 00:23:58.730
A doll without a heart,
born from warm hands

00:23:58.730 --> 00:24:08.240
I neither smile nor talk

00:24:08.240 --> 00:24:16.250
I want you to hear about
these feelings someday,

00:24:16.250 --> 00:24:24.430
though they can't be put into words

00:24:24.430 --> 00:24:32.430
I'll summon all my strength

00:24:32.430 --> 00:24:46.280
to know what it means to live

00:25:01.000 --> 00:25:06.010
"Flowers of Good Will"
